{
  "_id": "3AONCC6cssRWNTfGBx86XSB2Exn",
  "_type": "Docs",
  "_index": "a1",
  "title": "Tutorial",
  "navigationTitle": "Tutorial",
  "body": [
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Build a small but complete Next.js website with Alinea, one feature at a time. Each step adds to the code of the previous one and ends with a list of things you can check in the browser and the dashboard."
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": " The finished code of every step is in the repository at "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "apps/web/tutorial-sites",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_link": "url",
              "href": "https://github.com/alineacms/alinea/tree/main/apps/web/tutorial-sites",
              "_id": "3JlYEUQlJnJtoJ8Pw4HgjYUO9YF"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "orderedList",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Landing page",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "link",
                      "_id": "3JkCIs1Y6LDLL0oh5eXUkqLIwbA",
                      "_link": "entry",
                      "_entry": "3AONC8bWerkI4aXNcgz4fOm5Mxe"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": ": one fixed homepage entry with a title and SEO metadata, and live previews."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Content blocks",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "link",
                      "_id": "3JkCIxIdYXQnFJ1YyPF32VBU3XH",
                      "_link": "entry",
                      "_entry": "3AONCBGWB01JivtUHVnGHF3ICYf"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": ": a list of text, image and weather blocks that editors arrange freely."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Shared root",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "link",
                      "_id": "3JkCItprVqp4JFKLno5kuSd0swK",
                      "_link": "entry",
                      "_entry": "3AONCCkqtmD6746UsDgQ826GDp8"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": ": a settings root with the header and footer text used on every page."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Blog",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "link",
                      "_id": "3JkCIt3lrqX9YhtbkROHSkuYZvy",
                      "_link": "entry",
                      "_entry": "3AONC9h7c2NnMtmorYnCBd19LjN"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": ": a blog overview with nested posts, dedicated routes and previous/next links."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Catch-all route",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "link",
                      "_id": "3JkCItexoUkgbJBdiwlCFWQgi7P",
                      "_link": "entry",
                      "_entry": "3AONCEKYoMQiZ5HZWNKbMB8oVUT"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": ": one route that renders every page, so editors can build their own page tree."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Before you start"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "before-you-start"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Set up a Next.js project with Alinea by following the "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Quickstart",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JkCIx9AHRl4kCgRMtCh2BCq2PT",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "2YWqKUTrANlgEFMyBUEYdih2HpP"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": ": `alinea init` gives you the API route, the `dev` and `build` scripts and a `cms.ts` file that you replace in step 1. The tutorial uses the App Router, TypeScript and Next.js 16."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Conventions used in every step"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "conventions-used-in-every-step"
    },
    {
      "_type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "One folder per page type and block type.",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": " Each folder holds a schema file (`LandingPage.schema.tsx`) and a server component that renders it (`LandingPage.tsx`). Page types live in `entries/`, block types in `blocks/`."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Components fetch their own data.",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": " Every page component queries the entry it renders and exports its own `generateMetadata`. The files in `app/` stay thin and only pass route parameters along."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "The config is `cms.tsx` in the project root",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": ", and the `@/*` path alias in `tsconfig.json` points to the root, so imports read `@/cms` and `@/entries/...`. If your project keeps its code in `src/`, put these folders there instead."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Because each component loads its own data, you can make any of them a "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "cached component",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3AR0sSBtNppAOz9pfiIk8ZrUQCO",
              "_link": "url",
              "href": "https://nextjs.org/docs/app/getting-started/cache-components"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": " when it fits. Step 2 does this for a block that calls a weather API."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
